t of all we have a reactor  now the reactor is where we have these  uranium fuel rods that we were just  looking at a second ago so this is where  all of our fishing sorry this is where  all of our fishing reactions are  happening so lots and lots of energy is  being released  we also however have these things called  called  control rods now what a control rod is  is these are made out of boron and what  they're for is they absorb some of the  some neutrons so what we can do is if we  can help to control the rate that this  reaction these fission reactions are  happening by putting the control rods in  further or removing them because what  happens is as we've put a control rod in  they absorb some of these neutrons which  are being given off by these fission  reactions in order to slow the reaction  down so that is the purpose of the  control rods so we also have next to our  reactor we have  a boiler okay  now the whole purpose of the boiler is  to take all of this heat energy from the  reactor in order to to evaporate water  so we're turning water into steam so um  remember because during these fission  reactions we releasing loads and loads  of energy that energy can be used to  heat up water to turn it to steam this  theme can then go and turn a turbine  which can power a generator and in turn  generate electricity so we start off the  energy changes that are happening we  start off with nuclear energy lots as  these fission reactions occur we're  releasing lots of thermal energy which  in turns quick evaporates the water into  steam which then converts it into  kinetic energy in order to move the  turbine the turbine spins around and  then within a generator we have that  kinetic energy being converted into  electrical energy that is how nuclear  fishing works
 

